`JSON.parse` on package.json has no guard. A BOM (some Windows editors prepend U+FEFF), a trailing comma from a hand edit, or any malformed input throws a raw stack trace that prebuild/CI will surface without the file/line context anyone needs to debug. Add a try/catch with a clear message naming package.json and the underlying `err.message`.

```js
let pkg;
try {
  pkg = JSON.parse(readFileSync(pkgPath, 'utf8'));
} catch (err) {
  console.error(`[sync-version] 解析 ${pkgPath} 失败: ${err.message}`);
  process.exit(1);
}
```

The semver guard is too loose to actually achieve its stated goal of catching hand-typed mistakes. The `([-+].*)?$` tail accepts outright garbage — `1.0.0-`, `1.0.0+$$`, `1.0.0-anything goes`, `1.0.0-.` — all of which would be silently propagated into package.json and, eventually, into the shipped Tauri bundle's `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`. Tighten the pre-release / build identifier subpatterns per semver §10 (or require a stricter sanity check at minimum: dash/plus must be followed by at least one `[0-9A-Za-z-]` character). Suggested pragmatic tightening:

```js
if (!/^\d+\.\d+\.\d+(?:-(?:0|[1-9]\d*|[\da-z-]+\.[\da-z-]+)(?:\.(?:0|[1-9]\d*|[\da-z-]+\.[\da-z-]+))*)?(?:\+[\da-z-]+(?:\.[\da-z-]+)*)?$/i.test(version)) {
  console.error(`[sync-version] Cargo.toml version "${version}" 不是合法的 semver，请先修正`);
  process.exit(1);
}
```

