Mutex poisoning is silently recovered with `e.into_inner()` after only an `eprintln!`, in three production paths (register/stop of `SSE_WRITERS`, and `sse_connect`'s `hub.clients`). When a writer thread panics while mutating the registry or the clients list, the data structure may be in an inconsistent state (e.g., a partially-constructed `SseWriterReg`, a `tx`/`Weak` pair where only one was inserted). Continuing to push/remove on that inconsistent state can lead to duplicate registrations, lost stop signals, double-dropped senders, or audits that never fire. Either propagate the panic (let the process restart under whatever supervisor runs it) or, at minimum, refuse the operation and fail the request — do not keep mutating state that a previous panic may have corrupted.

Affected paths:
```rust
let mut g = SSE_WRITERS.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| {
    eprintln!("[mutex_poisoned] api_handlers::sse::SSE_WRITERS: {e:?}");
    e.into_inner()
});
```

