**Silent no-op on mutex poison in `scheduled_job_fire` pre-check**

`sched_running(&app).lock().map(|s| s.contains(&id)).unwrap_or(true)` collapses a poisoned mutex to "guard in progress", silently returning `Ok(())` to the Tauri caller without running the job. The Tauri command succeeds, no audit log is written, no error is surfaced, and the UI shows no feedback — the "立即执行" click appears to do nothing.

Suggest distinguishing "guard in progress" from "lock unavailable": log the poison (matching `SchedGuard::acquire`'s `eprintln!("[mutex_poisoned] ...")` pattern) and treat poison as `None` (skip silently is fine here only with an audit trail), or propagate as a `CommandError`.

