**Triple `db_load` per tick in `find_due_tasks`**

The function does an initial `db_load`, and then **reloads the entire tasks table twice more** (once for stale cleanup, once for missed handling) when either branch is non-empty. Worst case: 3 full `db_load` per tick × every 30s. This widens the window where concurrent user edits invalidate the snapshot, and on large task tables is a real cost.

Suggest: keep the original `all` in scope and reuse its `updated_at`/current values for the RMW baseline (the current "snapshot updated_at" semantics is what the code actually wants — re-loading to get a fresh `updated_at` is a defensible choice, but you can do the second/third UPDATE inline with the matched rows already in memory, avoiding both the second/third DB hit and the cross-edit race):

```rust
let mut stale_updates: Vec<Task> = Vec::new();
let mut missed_updates: Vec<Task> = Vec::new();
let mut due = Vec::new();
for mut t in all.into_iter() {
    // ... existing filters ...
    if /* stale */ {
        t.expected_updated_at = t.updated_at;
        t.schedule = None;
        t.updated_at = Some(now_ms);
        stale_updates.push(t);
    } else if /* missed */ {
        t.expected_updated_at = t.updated_at;
        t.sched_last = Some(now_ms);
        t.updated_at = Some(now_ms);
        missed_updates.push(t);
    } else if /* run */ { due.push(t); }
}
```

