**`sched_last` rollback RMW can silently fail under concurrent edits**

Both `run_scheduled_job` and `run_scheduled_workflow` write `sched_last = now` first, then if card creation / spawn fails they try to roll back by RMW with `expected_updated_at = Some(now.timestamp_millis())`. If any concurrent operation (another scheduler tick, user edit, frontend save) bumps `updated_at` between the two writes, the RMW returns 0 rows, the rollback silently fails, and the audit log only records "本次触发仍会丢弃". For an `at:` job/workflow this means the trigger is permanently lost — it's neither due anymore nor considered expired.

Suggest: detect the conflict distinctly from a real rollback success. When the rollback UPDATE matches 0 rows, re-read the row and decide: if `sched_last == now_ms` (some other path wrote the same sched_last — harmless), all good; if it's been overwritten by user edits, surface that explicitly (e.g., audit `sched_rollback_lost_to_concurrent_edit` and consider whether to re-arm the trigger or leave it to the next scan).

```rust
if !reverted {
    // 二次查证：RMW 失败可能是用户编辑而非真正的冲突
    if let Ok(cur) = crate::db::db_load(app.clone()).await {
        if let Some(row) = cur.into_iter().find(|t| t.id == job.id) {
            if row.sched_last != Some(now.timestamp_millis()) {
                crate::bot::audit_log(&app, &format!(
                    "sched_job_rollback_lost | id: {} | 并发编辑已覆盖 sched_last，at: 可能永久搁浅",
                    job.id
                ));
            }
        }
    }
}
