`route_user_input` holds the process-wide `RwLock` read guard across the full `match_compiled` loop. Patterns are sourced from installed skill frontmatter (skill-author controlled), and matching runs `Regex::is_match` over the entire user message text (including `[附件文件]` blocks). A slow pathological pattern (even though the `regex` crate guards against catastrophic backtracking, long inputs × many patterns still cost) blocks every `rebuild_routes` writer for the duration of one request, and a misconfigured skill can stall routing for the whole process. Snapshot the compiled rules into an owned `Vec` (or `Arc<Vec<CompiledRule>>` clone) and release the guard before matching, or move matching onto a thread-local that takes a short-lived clone.

```rust
pub fn route_user_input(text: &str) -> RouteAction {
    let guard = match ROUTES.read() {
        Ok(g) => g,
        Err(e) => e.into_inner(),
    };
    match_compiled(text, &guard)
}
