`cosine` recomputes the L2 norms on every call even though the contract documents that both vectors are already L2-normalized. With ~500 rows × 512 dims scanned on every `insert_item_with` and `load_all`, that is wasted work in the dedup hot path. Trust the contract and return the dot product directly (with the existing zero-norm guard via dot==0), or at minimum fast-path the already-normalized case.

