comments.content:
`MOVE_REMOVE_FAILS` uses a `HashMap<String, u32>` keyed by the raw `src` string, but Windows file paths are case-insensitive while `String` is case-sensitive. `C:\Users\Foo\bar` and `c:\users\foo\bar` will be stored as two distinct counters, so a single physical file's failure count can be reset merely by path normalization (Tauri/canoicalize/dunce-cap behavior, drive-letter casing, etc.). This silently defeats `MAX_MOVE_REMOVE_FAILURES` and re-enables the "archive directory accumulates copies of a permanently-locked source" failure mode this gate is supposed to prevent. Normalize the key (e.g. lowercase on Windows, `std::fs::canonicalize` then key by the canonical form) before insert/lookup, or use a path-aware key type.

```rust
fn normalize_src_key(src: &str) -> String {
    #[cfg(windows)] { src.to_lowercase() }
    #[cfg(not(windows))] { src.to_string() }
}
```

