Silent fallback on sidecar JSON parse failure. `read_to_string(&sidecar).ok().and_then(|s| serde_json::from_str::<WordTemplateParams>(&s).ok())` discards both I/O and parse errors, so a corrupted-but-readable `<name>.json` is indistinguishable from a missing one and silently re-harvested. This hides data corruption and produces drift if the harvest heuristic is later upgraded (old sidecar is treated as missing). Distinguish I/O from parse errors, and on parse failure either surface the error or audit it before falling through.

```rust
match std::fs::read_to_string(&sidecar) {
    Ok(s) => match serde_json::from_str::<WordTemplateParams>(&s) {
        Ok(v) => (Some(v), "params: saved"),
        Err(e) => {
            py_audit(app, &format!("doc_make_word 旁车参数解析失败 | {e}"));
            None  // fallthrough to harvest
        }
    },
    Err(_) => None,
}
```

