`WMESSAGE_EVAL_DB` is consumed verbatim (only `.trim()`) and used to open whatever SQLite file an outer process sets — combined with a hardcoded macOS-only fallback path that means any user/agent who wires this up in a script is implicitly trusting whoever set the env var. Validate (canonicalize, require suffix `.db`, refuse symbolic links to outside `~/Library/Application Support/com.renshi.wmessage/`), restrict to the default path, and remove the silent `~/Library/...` fallback so cross-platform/headless runs fail loud with a clear remediation message rather than silently locking onto whichever path matches first.

```rust
fn eval_db_path() -> Option<std::path::PathBuf> {
    let canonical_default = dirs::data_dir()?
        .join("com.renshi.wmessage")
        .join("wmessage.db");
    let p = std::env::var("WMESSAGE_EVAL_DB")
        .ok()
        .map(|s| s.trim().to_string())
        .filter(|s| !s.is_empty())
        .map(std::path::PathBuf::from)
        .map(|p| p.canonicalize().unwrap_or(p))
        .unwrap_or(canonical_default);
    // 必须存在、是普通文件、且位于默认库目录下（防 env var 误导读任意 SQLite）
    if !p.is_file() { return None; }
    let canon_default = canonical_default.canonicalize().ok()?;
    p.starts_with(canon_default.parent()?).then_some(p)
}
```

