`dueSoonTasks` only filters with `x.due <= horizon`, with no lower bound. A task due years ago that was never completed/archived will be surfaced indefinitely and pinned at the top of the list (sorted ascending). The doc says "7 天内会撞线的事" — old overdue items don't fit. Add a lower bound (e.g. `>= startOfToday.getTime() - 7 * 86_400_000`) or filter out very-old overdue items explicitly.

```ts
const startOfToday = new Date(now);
startOfToday.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);
const lowerBound = startOfToday.getTime() - 7 * 86_400_000;
// ...
.filter((x) => x.due >= lowerBound && x.due <= horizon)
```

The "Monday-as-week-start" computation `start.setDate(start.getDate() - ((start.getDay() + 6) % 7))` appears verbatim in both `weeklyBuckets` and `plannedTasksByDay`, plus a near-identical snippet in `archivePulse`. Extract a helper to keep week-rollover logic from drifting:

```ts
function startOfWeek(d: Date): Date {
  const s = new Date(d);
  s.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);
  s.setDate(s.getDate() - ((s.getDay() + 6) % 7));
  return s;
}
```

