comments.content:
`taRef` is a ref object — its identity is normally stable, so listing it in the dep array is misleading. If any caller ever creates a fresh `useRef` per render (or switches the ref binding), this effect will run every commit, rewriting `style.height` on the textarea each time and potentially causing caret flicker. Drop the ref from the dep array and capture the element via the `taRef.current` read at call time (the lint warning is expected here):

```ts
useEffect(() => {
  const ta = taRef.current;
  if (!ta) return;
  ta.style.height = "auto";
  ta.style.height = `${ta.scrollHeight}px`;
  // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps
}, [dep]);
```

Also note that `taRef.current` may be `null` on the first run; if so, the resize is silently skipped — consider a callback-ref or running once on mount.

