localStorage shim unconditionally overrides jsdom's implementation on Node 26. The guard `typeof globalThis.localStorage === "undefined"` is true both when the property is absent AND when Node 26 declares `globalThis.localStorage` with an `undefined` value (no `--localstorage-file`). When jsdom is then layered on top, the shim — installed at module-load time before jsdom's window is fully wired — masks the real jsdom Storage. Consequences: (a) no `storage` events fired across frames, (b) the in-memory `Map` survives across test files within a worker (jsdom is per-file), causing cross-test contamination from any previous test, (c) `beforeEach` `localStorage.clear()` calls reach the shim instead of jsdom's tracking, silently changing assumptions in tests like theme/WalletApp. Guard with `'localStorage' in globalThis` (in === present + value undefined is intentional capture) or, preferably, install only after jsdom has finished mounting (e.g., in a `beforeAll` after `vi.hoisted` or after importing a jsdom-touching module).

