comments.content:
Test isolation: globals installed here are write-once and never reset. `__TAURI_INTERNALS__` is the only one reseeded in `afterEach`; `window.matchMedia`, `globalThis.WebGL2RenderingContext`, `globalThis.WebGLRenderingContext`, the `localStorage` shim, and `crypto.randomUUID` survive forever. A single test that mutates any of them (e.g. `window.matchMedia = customImpl` to test SSR, or `localStorage.setItem('bootstrap', ...)` priming before component mount) leaks state to every subsequent test in the same file. The comment block above the scrollNoop reference even cites "原型链安全规则" against persisting patches — applying the same teardown discipline to these globals would prevent order-dependent flakes.

Existing code:
```js
afterEach(() => {
  cleanup();
  vi.restoreAllMocks();
  // errorHandler 的降级分支用例会显式 delete __TAURI_INTERNALS__（模拟纯浏览器），
  // 删除会残留到同文件后续用例——这里复位基线，保证每个用例都从 Tauri 宿主起步
  if (typeof window !== "undefined") {
    (window as unknown as Record<string, unknown>).__TAURI_INTERNALS__ = {};
  }
});
```

