Memory leak: `sessionUsage` Record is never pruned when a session is deleted. The sibling Maps (`drafts`, `filesBySession`, `effortBySession`) are all cleared in this block, but `sessionUsage` entries persist for deleted sessions forever. Long-running app with many deleted sessions = unbounded growth and inflated save payloads (each `bot_history_save` would eventually carry stale entries that map to nothing).

Add a matching cleanup for `sessionUsage` here, e.g.:

```ts
setSessionUsage((prev) => {
  const next = { ...prev };
  delete next[sid];
  return next;
});
```

