Memory leak on error path: `streamingMetaMapRef.current.delete(sid)` only runs in the success branch (the `try` body), but the `catch` branch still leaves the meta entry (thinking/tools/skillFailure/fileChanges) in the Map. Every failed `bot_chat` invocation leaks one entry per session indefinitely. Since `set(sid, {})` was called at the start of `runChat`, the entry exists whether or not the call succeeds.

Move the `delete(sid)` into a `finally` block (or just delete in `catch`) so the meta is always cleaned up:

```ts
} catch (e) {
  const failed: Msg[] = [...];
  persistHistory(sid, failed);
  if (sessionIdRef.current === sid) setMessages(failed);
  handleCommandError(e, "bot_chat", { silent: true });
} finally {
  streamingMetaMapRef.current.delete(sid);
  exitChat(sid);
}
```

