comments.content:
Crash risk: `rowsToMsgs` calls `JSON.parse` on `refsJson` / `toolsJson` without try/catch. The data is sourced from the Tauri backend (rows come from `bot_history_load`), and a single malformed payload will throw inside `rows.map`, escaping every outer `await ... .catch(handleCommandError(...))` (init / switchSession / openExecSession / deleteSession all expect `rowsToMsgs` to return, not throw). Result: history silently disappears for that session, with no user-visible error.

Wrap the parse in a safe helper that falls back to `undefined` on parse error:

```ts
const safeParse = <T,>(s: string | null | undefined): T | undefined => {
  if (!s) return undefined;
  try {
    return JSON.parse(s) as T;
  } catch {
    return undefined;
  }
};

const rowsToMsgs = (rows: ...): Msg[] =>
  rows.map((r) => ({
    role: r.role === "user" ? "user" : "assistant",
    content: r.content,
    refs: safeParse<TaskRef[]>(r.refsJson),
    thinking: r.thinking ?? undefined,
    tools: safeParse<ToolCall[]>(r.toolsJson),
  }));
```

