comments.content:
Race condition: the mount-load `useEffect([enabled])` runs an async IIFE with no `cancelled` flag / `AbortController`. If `enabled` flips false→true→false (e.g., bot toggle, widget remount, StrictMode double-invoke) before the first `bot_sessions_load` resolves, an older load can complete and `setSessions` / `setSessionId` / `setMessages` after a newer one has already populated state — the `sessionIdRef.current !== cur.id` guard inside only protects against later in-flight loads, not against the older one arriving last.

Add a cancellation flag (same pattern used by the drag-drop effect):

```ts
useEffect(() => {
  if (!enabled) return;
  let cancelled = false;
  (async () => {
    try {
      const list = await invoke<Session[]>("bot_sessions_load");
      if (cancelled) return;
      // ...rest
      if (sessionIdRef.current !== cur.id) return;
      if (cancelled) return;
      const rows = await invoke<...>("bot_history_load", { sessionId: cur.id });
      if (cancelled) return;
      if (sessionIdRef.current !== cur.id) return;
      if (rows?.length) setMessages(rowsToMsgs(rows));
    } catch (e) {
      handleCommandError(e, "chat init", { silent: true });
    }
  })();
  return () => {
    cancelled = true;
  };
}, [enabled]);
```

