Stale-UI / double-action risk: every mutation (`approveMemoryProposals`, `rejectMemoryProposals`, `enableEvolutionProposal`, `confirmArtifactBatch`, `respondWorkflowQuestion`, `dismissNotification`, `clearDoneNotifications`) only refreshes the list via the `NOTIFICATIONS_CHANGED_EVENT` listener. If that event is missed or delayed, the row still shows `status === "pending"` and the user can re-click and re-issue the same command (e.g. double-approving the same memory ids) — and `approveMemoryProposals` is called with the full ids list with no diff. Trigger a local `reload()` in the `finally` of each `act` (or set a per-card "removing" flag on success) as a belt-and-braces fallback.

