Minor UX/state bug in `WorkflowQuestionCard` answer derivation: `answerText = text.trim() || picked`. If the user picks a chip (`setPicked(opt); setText("")`) and then types a space (which `text.trim()` makes empty), the chip selection is silently dropped — but the "answer" button only just became enabled because `picked` was set. With trim+||, typing any whitespace also clears the chip selection invisibly. Use a more explicit precedence (e.g. prefer trimmed text only if non-empty, otherwise fall back to `picked`) and gate input so empty/whitespace typing doesn't clobber `picked`.

Existing context:
```tsx
  const options = Array.isArray(q.options) ? q.options : [];
  const answerText = text.trim() || picked;
