parseMemoryTuningInput silently accepts invalid values (negative numbers, 0, scientific notation, fractional values for `int` fields) and an all-empty form degrades to `tuning: null`, which the backend reads as "reset to defaults". A user who clears a single field and clicks 保存 will silently blow that parameter back to its default with the misleading "已保存" message. Add explicit validation per field (range, min, and enforce integer for `int: true` via Number.isInteger(n) after parseFloat/parseInt) and either disallow an all-empty submit or require a separate "reset to defaults" action with confirmation.

Existing code:
function parseMemoryTuningInput(
  raw: Record<string, string>,
): Record<string, number> | null {
  const out: Record<string, number> = {};
  for (const f of MEMORY_TUNING_FIELDS) {
    const v = raw[f.key]?.trim();
    if (!v) continue;
    const n = f.int ? parseInt(v, 10) : parseFloat(v);
    if (Number.isFinite(n)) out[f.key] = n;
  }
  return Object.keys(out).length > 0 ? out : null;
}

