Stale coordinates captured at pointer entry: `getBoundingClientRect()` runs immediately on `show`, but the tip only renders 350ms later. If the page scrolls, the host element moves (e.g., due to layout shifts, virtualization, or the host re-rendering) during the delay, the chip appears at outdated `x`/`y`, frequently disconnected from the trigger or even pointing at unrelated elements. Capture the rect inside the `setTimeout` callback (or recompute on render) and also close the tip on scroll.

```tsx
timer.current = setTimeout(() => {
  const r = (e.currentTarget as HTMLElement).getBoundingClientRect();
  setTip({ text, x: r.left, y: r.top });
}, 350);
```

