comments.content:
Returned handlers are fresh closures on every render. Consumers wiring `onPointerEnter={show(...)}` / `onPointerLeave={hide}` or passing them into memoized children/effects will see referential changes each render, defeating downstream `React.memo`/`useCallback`/`useEffect` optimizations. Wrap with `useCallback`, and memoize the curried `show(text)` per text so the same host element gets a stable handler reference.

```tsx
const show = useCallback((text: string) => (e: React.PointerEvent) => { ... }, []);
const hide = useCallback(() => { ... }, []);
```

