plannedTasks uses `!!t.planStart && !!t.planEnd`, but a JavaScript `Invalid Date` (e.g. `new Date("garbage")`) is a non-null object and therefore truthy. Such tasks will pass the filter, then `segsForWeek` and `layoutLanes` will propagate `NaN` into the inline `top`/`height` styles, silently producing empty/corrupt block positions. Guard with `!isNaN(t.planStart.getTime())` (and the same for `planEnd`) instead of relying on object truthiness.

